# Plan 001: v000 runtime gate (Kaggle L4x4, E4B first, then 31B). Pre-registered 2026-11-04, before any run.
Decision: ops/decisions/002.
## Hypothesis
v000 bundles run end to end in the scorer environment, produce a non-empty source diff, never edit tests, keep scratch outside /workspace, and fit the time budget.
## Measurements (dev tasks only; concurrency 1; Kaggle L4x4)
vLLM startup time; sandbox setup time per task; per-task wall time (n ~5-8 for timing, >=2 for smoke); tokens/sec; non-empty-diff rate; test-file edits (must be 0); stray files in /workspace (must be 0). No pass-rate claims (n too small).
## Prerequisite (CPU, no GPU quota)
Gold calibration on this VM via bin/job: apply gold patch + test_patch, run pytest, keep passers as clean list (hash recorded); split clean tasks by repo into dev/holdout, freeze in eval/splits/, journal hashes. No tuning on holdout.
## Decision rule
Cap check uses p90 per-task wall time: pass iff p90*125 + startup <= 660 min AND cap_minutes*125+30 <= 660. Else lower caps in eval_config.yaml, repack, re-measure. E4B passing smoke+timing => report 002 with SUBMIT request for e4b-v000 as baseline. Any test edit or empty-diff on a smoke task => fix before submit.
## Quota budget
<= 10 L4x4 hours this week (resets Sat 2026-11-07 00:00 UTC), <= 4 h per session, chunked/resumable. Logged in ops/budget/kaggle.md. GCP spend: $0.
## Addendum 2026-11-05 (dec 013 M3; measurement only, decision rule unchanged)
Participant evidence (thread 752017): local timing on public repos underestimated test-run cost on hidden repos. Add to measurements: per-task time share spent in test-running tool calls (pytest/run_tests wall time / task wall time), reported as mean and p90, plus the count of test runs per task. Keep the p90 rule as written. In the report, flag the test-run share as a risk term: if it is large, the hidden-repo worst case may exceed our local p90, so cap test runs per task in the bundle rather than relying only on cap_minutes.
